.TH CPN 1 "2026-08" "chopin 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cpn \- copy files and directories
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cpn
[\fIOPTION\fR]... [\fB\-T\fR] \fISOURCE\fR \fIDEST\fR
.br
.B cpn
[\fIOPTION\fR]... \fISOURCE\fR... \fIDIRECTORY\fR
.br
.B cpn
[\fIOPTION\fR]... \fB\-t\fR \fIDIRECTORY\fR \fISOURCE\fR...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cpn
is the
.BR chopin (1)
binary installed under a shorter name. The two are the same program:
the invoked name changes only the prefix on diagnostics, so
.B cpn
reports errors as
.RI \(dq cpn : ...\(dq
where
.B chopin
reports
.RI \(dq chopin : ...\(dq.
.PP
Options, behavior, exit status, environment variables, and the
deviation register are documented in
.BR chopin (1).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR chopin (1),
.BR cp (1)
